## Late-session blockers found AND fixed (after the main session memo above)

Polina's live SS-S15-E01 smoke (right before /clear) surfaced two production blockers. Both already fixed:

- **`e5ffa22` + migration 0034** — Schema `assets_file_type_check` rejected uppercase in shot-id variants. All 22 Designer jobs failed at INSERT. Relaxed regex `[a-z0-9_-]+` → `[A-Za-z0-9_-]+`. Migration applied to production.
- **`cdb7f9f`** — `approve/route.ts` REV-world_check.APPROVED fan-outed all 22 shots as Designer events. Director: «должны запуститься первых два пилотных как всегда было». Fix: `PILOT_COUNT_DESIGNER=2`, remaining shot ids stashed in `episodes.metadata.designer_fanout_pending`. Mirror EREF v2 pattern.

After these fixes:
- `next-dev` was restarted (serverId `fb9a2ed9-9b9d-45ab-8b0f-f930fc26bef6` at /clear time)
- Polina notified via team-chat (turns `76a6b1ad` for schema fix, `90f796aa` for pilot fix)
- No active generation jobs (all 22 failed quickly at schema CHECK, then I fixed both blockers)
- Director chose to clear context before deciding how to resume the smoke

**TD-23 (new, logged in PLAN.md)** — Designer post-pilot auto-fanout-trigger. After 2 pilots are approved, remaining shot ids (20 in our case) need to fire as additional Designer plan events. Currently manual via `triggerAgent('EXEC-EREF-DESIGNER', {shotId})` per stashed id. ~2-3h to implement properly (mirror `sandystudio/exec-eref/fanout-trigger` pattern).

